is unreachable for batching FSMs, an application that implements both interfaces silently loses the only library-provided delivery of committed configuration changes, which matters for recovery and for the FSM's own view of cluster membership. This is an implementation/contract gap, not a consensus-safety violation; it is classified implementation_semantics.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"S34\",\n    \"S35\",\n    \"S36\",\n    \"S37\",\n    \"S38\",\n    \"S8\",\n    \"S21\",\n    \"S24\"\n   ],\n   \"participants\": [\n    \"leader or follower main thread\",\n    \"FSM goroutine\",\n    \"application FSM\"\n   ],\n   \"objects\": [\n    \"Raft.runFSM / applySingle / applyBatch\",\n    \"ConfigurationStore.StoreConfiguration\",\n    \"BatchingFSM.ApplyBatch\",\n    \"a FSM implementing both interfaces\"\n   ],\n   \"contexts\": [\n    \"committed LogConfiguration entry applied after a membership change\",\n    \"batched commit delivery when the FSM implements BatchingFSM\"\n   ],\n   \"event_paths\": [\n    \"AddVoter/RemoveServer -> appendConfigurationEntry -> dispatchLogs -> commit -> processLogs -> fsmMutateCh -> applyBatch\",\n    \"AddVoter/RemoveServer -> appendConfigurationEntry -> dispatchLogs -> commit -> processLogs -> fsmMutateCh -> applySingle -> StoreConfiguration\"\n   ],\n   \"activity_classes\": [\n    \"A1\",\n    \"A5\",\n    \"A6\"\n   ],\n   \"behavior_ids\": [\n    \"b-fsm-apply-committed\"\n   ],\n   \"fact_ids\": [\n    \"f-fsm-configuration-state\"\n   ],\n   \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n    \"b-append-entries-sync\": \"A1 relationship: the configuration fact consumed during AppendEntries processing is the same configuration whose FSM-side persistence this question investigates; the FSM record is an alternative establishment path for the context that determines voter eligibility and therefore qualified support for advancement.\",\n    \"b-recover-from-disk\": \"Explains why the missing del\nunits: [{\"id\": \"unit-claim-config-store-delivery\", \"candidate_id\": \"831856452d6b4e1985b8de082764a214\", \"obligation_ids\": [\"claim-config-store-delivery\"], \"binding_ids\": [\"binding-config-store-delivery\"], \"relation_ids\": [], \"scope\": {\"description\": \"A single Raft node whose FSM implements ConfigurationStore, processing a committed LogConfiguration entry. The obligation concerns delivery of the configuration entry to the FSM, not the correctness of the configuration value itself.\", \"assumptions\": [\"The entry has been committed (reached the FSM via processLogs).\", \"The FSM implements ConfigurationStore as documented in configuration.go:44-52.\"], \"excluded\": [\"Whether ApplyBatch is the intended delivery point for batching FSMs is a separate contract question; this claim only asserts the Configuratio\nclaims: [{\"id\": \"claim-config-store-delivery\", \"kind\": \"obligation\", \"concern\": \"implementation_semantics\", \"description\": \"For every FSM that implements ConfigurationStore, the library must invoke StoreConfiguration(index, configuration) for each committed configuration log entry that it delivers to the FSM, so that a persistent FSM can reconstruct configuration without an external snapshot.\", \"scope\": {\"description\": \"A single Raft node whose FSM implements ConfigurationStore, processing a committed LogConfiguration entry. The obligation concerns delivery of the configuration entry to the FSM, not the correctness of the configuration value itself.\", \"assumptions\": [\"The entry has been committed (reached the FSM via processLogs).\", \"The FSM implements ConfigurationStore as documented in configura\npending_work: [{\"id\": \"unit-claim-config-store-delivery\", \"candidate_id\": \"831856452d6b4e1985b8de082764a214\", \"kind\": \"unit\", \"remaining\": [\"claim-config-store-delivery\"], \"record\": {\"path\": \"state.json\", \"collection\": \"units\", \"match\": {\"id\": \"unit-claim-config-store-delivery\"}}}]\nreview_contracts: []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
